FeeBL output files

Outputs depend on the selected processes and storage switches. Retain acc.dat,
the complete stdout/stderr log, and the actual executable with each run.
out.dat (or the third positional argument) contains evaluated input settings
and integrated results. The benchmark runner additionally writes execution.json,
stdout.txt, stderr.txt and their combined log.txt. The following legacy files
retain GUINEA-PIG++ conventions except where extensions are stated.

1) photon.dat:
   
   It contains the photons after the interaction.

   Photon Energy [GeV] |  angle x [rad] |  angle y [rad] 

   If the energy is negative the photon is from the second beam.	

2) beam1(2).dat
   
   Particles of the first and second beam respectively.

   Particle Energy [GeV] | x [um] | y [um] | z [um] | x' [urad] | y' [urad]

3) coh1(2).dat 
   
   Coherent Pairs of the first and second beam respectively.
   
   Particle Energy [GeV] | x [um] | y [um] | z [um] | x' [mrad] | y' [mrad]

4) pairs.dat 
  
   Incoherent Pairs after beam-beam interaction.
   
   Signed Energy [GeV] | Beta_x | Beta_y | Beta_z | x [nm] | y [nm] | z [nm] | process (*) | source slice 1 | source slice 2

   (*) 'process' can be:
       	'0' : Breit-Wheeler
	'1' : Bethe-Heitler
	'2' : Landau-Lifschitz

   Column 8 is the process code, not a statistical weight. Positive energy
   identifies an electron and negative energy a positron. The records depend
   on generation thresholds, tracking and storage thinning. Their row count
   is not generally the physical number of produced pairs. Imported-event
   identities are carried by the separate trajectory/spin outputs below.

5) hadron.dat

   Colliding photons that produced a hadronic event. 
   Since the number of these events is small per bunch crossing the number
   will be enhanced by a factor hadron_ratio.
  
   Photon Energy beam1 [GeV] | Photon Energy beam2 [GeV] | z of collision [um]

6) lumi.ee.out

   Colliding particles infos. do_lumi=1 e-e collision.
   energy of the colliding particles 
   position of the collision within the bunch 
   value of "time counter" of the collision
   normalized velocities of the colliding particles
   polarization vector of colliding particles (px1(2),py1(2),pz1(2))
   label 

   Energy beam1 [GeV] | Energy beam2 [GeV] | x [nm] | y [nm] | z [um] | Px1/E1 | Py1/E1 | Px2/E2 | Py2/E2 | px1 | py1 | pz1 | px2 | py2 | pz2 | label

7) Self-describing luminosity output (store_native=1):

   lumi.ee.out.fne contains stored collision records with schema metadata.
   lumi.ee.out.dLdW.fne contains weighted native collision-energy bins and
   helicity moments. Its header specifies columns, units and the uncertainty
   convention; encounter-based effective counts are not independent-run errors.
   lumi.ee.out.design_axis_dLdW.fne is the optional design-axis diagnostic.
   It transforms collision momenta without changing the existing weights and
   is not a replacement finite-angle collision or flux calculation.

8) Native viewer output (--make_gui_files):

   gui_b1.N and gui_b2.N contain deterministic sampled beam states at frame N.
   gui_manifest.raw.json binds frame identities, evaluated parameters and RNG
   checkpoint provenance. gui_diagnostics.json stores native moments and
   optional field-evaluation, photon and pair histograms. gui_fields.json
   stores sampled field layers; gui_mesh_coverage.json records domain coverage.
   gui_secondary_frames.json stores interval/final secondary distributions.
   gui_imported_trajectories.json stores identified imported-track histories.
   These files are conditional on supported output paths. A missing process
   is distinct from a computed population with zero entries.

   tools/finalize_gui_dataset.py validates the native files and produces
   gui_manifest.json plus derived viewer datasets, with source/binary hashes,
   normalization provenance and fit status. The manifest lists every served
   file. A finalized dataset is not evidence of numerical convergence.
   See docs/COLLIDER_GUI.md for frame weighting, display units and exports.

9) imported_spin.json (imported_spin_mode=1):

   Initial/final phase space, spin and helicity for explicitly identified
   imported electron/positron tracks, including field-sampling diagnostics.
   This radiation-off BMT mode is described in docs/IMPORTED_SPIN.md. It is
   independent of the smaller GUI trajectory-sampling limit.

10) rndm.save (rndm_save=1):

   Versioned, checksummed complete random-number state, including the Gaussian
   cache. An explicit rndm_load=1 restores it in preference to rndm_seed.
   Both switches default to zero. Failed or incompatible loads stop the run;
   see docs/RNG_CHECKPOINTS.md for transactional and portability guarantees.

 
